  "description": "<div>\n<p>In a binary tree, a path begins at the root and ends at a leaf (a node with no children). Find every such path whose node values add to <code>targetSum</code>. The tree is supplied as a level-order array with <code>null</code> slots for missing children.</p>\n<p>Return values along each path from root to leaf, and sort the list of paths lexicographically by numeric values (shorter matching prefixes first). An empty tree has no root-to-leaf paths.</p>\n<p><strong>Example 1:</strong></p>\n<pre><strong>Input:</strong> root = [5,4,8,11,null,13,4,7,2,null,null,5,1], targetSum = 22\n<strong>Output:</strong> [[5,4,11,2],[5,8,4,5]]\n<strong>Explanation:</strong> Two leaves complete a sum of 22, on the left and the right.</pre>\n<p><strong>Example 2:</strong></p>\n<pre><strong>Input:</strong> root = [1,2,3], targetSum = 4\n<strong>Output:</strong> [[1,3]]\n<strong>Explanation:</strong> Only the path from 1 to 3 reaches 4.</pre>\n<p><strong>Example 3:</strong></p>\n<pre><strong>Input:</strong> root = [], targetSum = 0\n<strong>Output:</strong> []\n<strong>Explanation:</strong> An empty tree has no leaves.</pre>\n<p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>0 &lt;= number of nodes &lt;= 100</code></li>\n<li><code>-100 &lt;= node value &lt;= 100</code></li>\n<li><code>-10,000 &lt;= targetSum &lt;= 10,000</code></li>\n</ul>\n</div>",
